# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zydit TTS — environment schema
#
# HOW TO USE
#   • Local development : copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in values.
#                         (`cp .env.example .env.local`)
#   • Cloudflare Pages  : Dashboard → your project → Settings →
#                         Environment variables → add each variable for BOTH
#                         Production and Preview, then redeploy.
#
# TWO KINDS OF VARIABLES — the distinction matters:
#   • VITE_*  → embedded in the client bundle. ANY visitor can read these
#               in their browser DevTools. Only put public values here.
#   • TTS_*   → server-side only (read by the /api/speech Pages Function).
#               These NEVER reach the browser — put your real API key and
#               real model ID here. Never prefix them with VITE_.
#
# SECURITY NOTES
#   • Never commit `.env.local` — it is gitignored.
#   • The real upstream endpoint, API key, and raw model ID belong in the
#     TTS_* variables, served through the same-origin proxy. Users only
#     ever see "ElevenLabs Multilingual v2" in the UI.
#   • End-user API keys are NEVER set here — in unmanaged mode users paste
#     their own key in the in-app API Settings dialog (sessionStorage only).
#
# SIGN-IN GATING: controlled in the frontend at `src/config.ts`
# (REQUIRE_SIGN_IN). Google sign-in must be configured (VITE_FIREBASE_*)
# while the gate is on.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Managed API proxy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to "true" to route ALL generation through the same-origin
# POST /api/speech Pages Function (functions/api/speech.ts). The function
# injects the real endpoint, API key, and model ID server-side, so none of
# them are ever visible in the browser. Users see a "Managed API" note in
# API Settings and never need to paste anything.
VITE_MANAGED_API="true"

# Server-side secrets for the /api/speech proxy (NOT VITE_ — stays on the
# server). Base URL of your OpenAI-compatible speech endpoint; the proxy
# appends /v1/audio/speech automatically if missing:
#   TTS_API_BASE_URL="https://your-gateway.example.com"
TTS_API_BASE_URL=""

# Bearer key for the upstream endpoint. Sent ONLY from the Pages Function
# to your gateway — never included in any client response.
TTS_API_KEY=""

# The REAL model ID your gateway should call. The UI always displays
# "ElevenLabs Multilingual v2" regardless of what this is set to.
TTS_MODEL_ID="eleven_multilingual_v2"

# ── Unmanaged mode (optional fallback) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Only used when VITE_MANAGED_API is not "true": the default endpoint users
# generate against (they can override it in the in-app API Settings dialog).
# The endpoint must send CORS headers — api.elevenlabs.io itself does not.
VITE_TTS_API_BASE_URL=""

# ── Firebase Auth (Google sign-in) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy these from: Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps →
# Web app config. Full walkthrough: docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md
#
# Auth is ENABLED only when API KEY, AUTH DOMAIN, PROJECT ID and APP ID are
# all present.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN="your-project.firebaseapp.com"
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project"
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET="your-project.appspot.com"
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""
